    {
      "title": "India to have one of the 'best' trade deals with the US: Piyush Goyal",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/economy/news/india-to-have-one-of-the-best-trade-deals-with-the-us-piyush-goyal-126111201505_1.html",
      "description": "Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal on Thursday said India will have one of the \"best\" trade deals with the US in every respect.\nHe said that India has negotiated a very good set of outcomes with the US in the pact.\n\"And in every respect, India will have one of the best deals with the US,\" he told reporters here.\nIndia and the US in February finalised a framework for the first phase of the bilateral trade agreement. However, changes in the tariff landscape in the US have led to further negotiations.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-12T17:38:27"
    },
    {
      "title": "India, Canada trade pact talks may conclude by Dec, says Canadian Minister",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/india-canada-trade-pact-talks-may-conclude-by-dec-says-canadian-minister-126111200965_1.html",
      "description": "Canadian Minister of International Trade Maninder Sidhu on Thursday said negotiations are on between India and Canada for a trade pact and expressed the hope that these talks will conclude by the time Prime Minister Narendra Modi visits Canada next month.\nIndia and Canada are currently holding the sixth round negotiations for the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement (CEPA).\n\"We're negotiating right now with India. I'm here for Round Six between our chief negotiators, and we're going to hopefully get there by the time Prime Minister Modi Ji visits Canada next month,\" he said here at a session of CII Partnership Summit.\nSidhu is here to attend the summit and also held discussions on the pact with Commerce and Industry Minister Piyush Goyal.\nBetween India and Canada, he said it's not about competition, it's about complementarities between the two economies.\nThe talks are moving at a faster pace as both the countries are targeting to conclude the negotiations by the end of thi",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-11-12T10:26:03"
    }
  ]
